# SHELLHACKS PROJECT CONTEXT & RULES

## TECH STACK
- Frontend: React (Vite), Leaflet.js (`react-leaflet`), CSS Modules / Standard CSS, `@google/genai` SDK.
- Backend: Python (FastAPI), `yfinance`, pandas, numpy, uvicorn.
- Deployment: Vercel (Frontend), Railway (Backend).

## REPOSITORY STRUCTURE
- `/frontend` -> All React code lives here.
- `/backend` -> All Python / FastAPI code lives here.

## GENERAL CODING RULES
1. NEVER generate code that modifies files outside of the target working directory (`/frontend` or `/backend`).
2. Always write clean, production-ready code with complete logic (NO placeholders, NO `// TODO: implement later` comments).
3. Keep frontend calls to Gemini inside direct React SDK calls using `import.meta.env.VITE_GEMINI_API_KEY`.
4. Ensure all map components inside Leaflet have explicit height/width CSS styles.
5. Write functional components using modern React hooks (`useState`, `useEffect`, `useRef`).

## DESIGN SYSTEM
- Theme: Dark institutional-grade financial terminal (Bloomberg / Refinitiv inspired).
- Palette: Dark slate gray (`#121212`), muted border grays (`#2A2A2A`), accent cyan/gold for interactive nodes.
